From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Send sooner with x264

The receiver trailed the desktop visibly when playing video. With x264 the
pipeline latency was 150 ms (patch 0017), and measured with sound included a
frame left about 100 to 116 ms after capture. At 80 ms it leaves about 35 ms
after capture, and the frames leave no less evenly: the spread between them
comes from the sound arriving in 40 ms periods, not from the latency. At
60 ms the largest gap between two frames grew to 100 ms in one of three
runs, so 80 ms is kept.

A frame that reaches the sink after its time is still sent at once, so the
drop budget of patch 0019 stays at 100 ms.

diff -ruN a/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c b/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
--- a/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
+++ b/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
@@ -340,9 +340,9 @@
   encoding_perf = gst_element_factory_make ("identity", "wfd-measure-encoder-realtime");
   success &= gst_bin_add (bin, encoding_perf);
   qos_data = g_new0 (QOSData, 1);
-  /* x264 runs with zero latency tuning and a 150 ms pipeline latency, so a
-   * frame 100 ms after capture is still sent in time. The other encoders
-   * keep the 50 ms they had. */
+  /* x264 runs with zero latency tuning and a short pipeline latency, and a
+   * frame that is late at the sink is still sent at once, so dropping is
+   * kept for frames far behind. The other encoders keep the 50 ms they had. */
   if (wfd_media_factory_profiles[self->factory_profile].video_encoder == ELEMENT_X264)
     qos_data->budget = 100 * GST_MSECOND;
   else
@@ -585,9 +585,11 @@
    * Every packet is sent that much after it was captured, so the latency is
    * felt as the receiver lagging behind the desktop. x264 is configured for
    * zero latency with no lookahead and no B-frames, and does not have those
-   * spikes, so it gets a much shorter one. */
+   * spikes, so it gets a much shorter one: measured with sound included,
+   * 80 ms sends a frame about 35 ms after capture, where 150 ms took over
+   * 100 ms, and the frames leave no less evenly. */
   if (encoder == ELEMENT_X264)
-    gst_pipeline_set_latency (GST_PIPELINE (pipeline), 150 * GST_MSECOND);
+    gst_pipeline_set_latency (GST_PIPELINE (pipeline), 80 * GST_MSECOND);
   else
     gst_pipeline_set_latency (GST_PIPELINE (pipeline), 500 * GST_MSECOND);
 
